'''''Capsella rubella''''', the '''pink shepherd's-purse''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> is a plant species in the genus ''[[Capsella (plant)|Capsella]]'', and a member of the [[mustard family]]. It has a very similar appearance to [[Capsella bursa-pastoris|''C.&nbsp;bursa-pastoris'']], but ''C.&nbsp;rubella'' has a [[diploid]] as opposed to a [[tetraploid]] genome.<ref>{{cite book|editor-last=Kawano|editor-first=Shoichi|title=Biological approaches and evolutionary trends in plants|date=1990|publisher=Academic Press|location=London|isbn=978-0-12-402960-6}}</ref> The species is also a very close relative of ''[[Arabidopsis thaliana]]''.<ref name="Stace-2019">{{cite book|last=Stace|first=C. A.|author-link = Stace, C. A.|year=2019|title=New Flora of the British Isles|edition=Fourth|publisher=C & M Floristics|location = Middlewood Green, Suffolk, U.K.| isbn=978-1-5272-2630-2}}</ref>{{rp|420}}

The separation of ''C.&nbsp;rubella'' from its closest ancestor (connecting it to ''[[Capsella grandiflora|C.&nbsp;grandiflora]]'') is theorized to have happened around 30,000 to 50,000 years ago.<ref name=guo>{{cite journal |last1=Guo |first1=Y.-L. |last2=Bechsgaard |first2=J.&nbsp;S. |last3=Slotte |first3=T. |last4=Neuffer |first4=B. |last5=Lascoux |first5=M. |last6=Weigel |first6=D. |last7=Schierup |first7=M.&nbsp;H. |year=2009 |title=Recent speciation of ''Capsella rubella'' from ''Capsella grandiflora'', associated with loss of self-incompatibility and an extreme bottleneck |url=https://uu.diva-portal.org/smash/get/diva2:210636/FULLTEXT01 |journal=[[Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences]] |volume=106 |issue=13 |pages=5246–5251 |bibcode=2009PNAS..106.5246G |doi=10.1073/pnas.0808012106 |pmc=2659713 |pmid=19307580 |doi-access=free}}</ref> Along with ''C.&nbsp;grandiflora,'' it is used as a [[model plant]] to study the evolution of [[self-incompatibility]] into self-compatibility in [[plant reproduction]].<ref name=guo/>

The species is found mostly in the [[Mediterranean region]].<ref name=POWO>{{cite web |work=Plants of the World Online |title=Capsella rubella Reut. |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:280061-1 }}</ref>

